000200 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000300 PROGRAM-ID.          TIRSNGL.
000400 AUTHOR.              C HILLES.
000500 DATE-WRITTEN.        7/1/83.
000600 DATE-COMPILED.
000700 INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
000800 SECURITY.
000900*REMARKS.             SINGLE ISSUE AND RETURN SUBPROGRAM.
001000*
001100*    ON NOVEMBER 15, 1983, CHANGED PRINT ROUTINE TO FORM FEED
001200*    TWICE AFTER THE PRINTOUT IS DONE.  THIS IS FOR 5.5 INCH
001300*    PAPER.  FORM LENGTH ON PRINTER MUST NOW BE SET TO 5.5.
001400*    ONLY GADSDEN AND DANVILLE HAVE THE HALF SHEETS NOW.
001500*
001600*    ON NOVEMBER 18, 1983, ADDED LAWTON TO THE HALF-SHEET
001700*    PLANTS.  CIH.
001800*
001900*    ON NOVEMBER 30, 1983, CHANGED PARAMETERS FOR CALL TO
002000*    "TSPLPRT".  NOW RETURNS ENTIRE SPOOLER REC, BUT NO
002100*    MESSAGE BUFFER.  CIH.
002200*
002300*    ON FEBRUARY 10, 1983, CHANGED PARAMETERS FOR CALL TO
002400*    "TREQFILU".  THE FIELDS "STR-RESERVED" AND "
002500*    "SAVE-RSRVD-BEFORE" WERE ADDED.  THIS IS BECAUSE THE
002600*    REQFILE UPDATE SUBPROGRAM WILL NOW CREATE AUTO REQS ON THE
002700*    BASIS OF AVAILABLE RATHER THAN ONHAND.  CIH.
002800*
002900*    ON APRIL 26, 1984, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
003000*    1. CHANGED PARAMETERS TO INCLUDE ENTIRE
003100*       SPOOLER REC (USER, ACCOUNT, TERM NUMBER, AND ALL 5 SPOOLER
003200*       NUMBERS), RATHER THAN JUST SPOOL-PRT.  THIS IS BECAUSE THE
003300*       5TH SPOOLER NUMBER WAS USED TO DETERMINE WHETHER HALF-SHEET,
003400*       PAPER WAS BEING USED, BUT THIS KEY WAS LOST WHEN GOING
003500*       BETWEEN SUB-PROGRAMS.  CIH.
003600*
003700*    ON AUGUST 10, 1984, CHANGED THE "DDAILYTC-LIST" TO
003800*    "ALL-ITEMS", BECAUSE WE CHANGED THE DATA ITEMS IN THE
003900*    DDAILYTC DATA-SET, AND ALL PLANTS DO NOT YET HAVE THE
004000*    CHANGE.  CIH.
004100*
004200*    ON SEPT 10, 1984, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
004300*      1.  ADDED A "BASE" PARAMETER FOR THE CALL TO "TREQFILU".
004400*          THIS IS BECAUSE THE KSAM FILE "REQFILE" IS GOING
004500*          TO BE ELIMINATED AND THE DATA PUT IN A NEW DATA
004600*          SEGMENT IN THE STORES DATABASE.  THE REQFILE FILE
004700*          NUMBER PARAMETER IS LEFT IN THE CALL SO THAT PROGRAMS
004800*          WILL WORK ON EITHER THE KSAM REQFILE OR THE DATABASE
004900*          REQFILE (SINCE "TREQFILU" IS IN THE ACCOUNT SL, NO
005000*          DIFFERENT VERSIONS OF PROGRAMS WILL HAVE TO BE
005100*          MAINTAINED FOR PLANTS THAT HAVE NOT YET MADE THE
005200*          DATABASE CHANGE).
005300*
005400*      2.  TOOK OUT THE OPEN OF THE KSAM FILE "REQFILE", AND ALL
005500*          THE KSAM WORK AREAS.  FROM NOW ON, THE OLD VERSION
005600*          OF "TREQFILU" (KSAM VERSION) WILL OPEN THE REQFILE
005700*          IF THE PASSED FILE NUMBER IS 0, THEN WILL RETURN THE
005800*          FILE NUMBER OF THE OPENED FILE.  THIS WAY THE FILE
005900*          WILL BE OPENED ONLY ONCE.  (THERE WILL BE NO FORMAL
006000*          CLOSE OF THE REQFILE).  FOR THE NEW VERSION OF
006100*          "TREQFILU" (DATABASE VERSION), OF COURSE NO KSAM
006200*          OPEN WILL BE NEEDED (AND THE REQFILE FILE NUMBER
006300*          PASSED WILL BE IGNORED). CIH.
006400*
006500*    ON OCT 8, 1984, CHANGED THIS SUBPROGRAM TO WORK FOR BOTH
006600*    THE AKRON PLANTS AND THE SUB-PLANTS.  FORMERLY THERE WAS
006700*    A SEPERATE VERSION OF ALL THE STORES PROGRAMS FOR AKRON
006800*    PLANTS.  THIS INVOLVED THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
006900*        1.  THE "DEFAULT EXPENSE CLASS" LOGIC WAS MOVED FROM
007000*            THIS SUBPROGRAM INTO THE "TIREDIT" EDITING SUB-
007100*            PROGRAM.  THIS REQUIRED ADDING THE "STR-EXP-CLASS"
007200*            AS A PARAMETER TO THE CALL OF "TIREDIT".
007300*            (DEFAULT EXP CLASS IS NOT USED IN AKRON, AND THE
007400*            EDITING SUB-PROGRAM WILL HANDLE THESE DIFFERENCES).
007500*
007600*        2.  AN "IF AKRON" STATEMENT WAS ADDED FOR UPDATING OF
007700*            LAST CHARGE DEPT.  THE STORES PROGRAMS ARE USED
007800*            FOR Z, IT, J BILLS, MATERIAL TRANSFERS, AND SPECIAL
007900*            STORES ISSUES.  IN THESE CASES, DIFFERENT FIELDS
008000*            MAY UPDATE "STR-LAST-CHARGE" OTHER THAN THE CHARGE
008100*            DEPT FIELD.  HOPEFULLY, SOON THESE FUNCTIONS WILL
008200*            BE MOVED OUT OF THE STORES PROGRAMS TO A SEPERATE
008300*            PROGRAM (WHERE THEY SHOULD BE).  AT THIS TIME THIS
008400*            LOGIC WILL BE REMOVED.
008500*
008600*        3.  THE "TIREDIT", "TQTYEDIT", "TWSPRT" SUBPROGRAMS WERE
008700*            CHANGED WITH SPECIAL LOGIC FOR AKRON.
008800*
008900*        4.  IN THE PRINT ROUTINE, IF AKRON A "CENTER" HEADING
009000*            IS ADDED FOR THE WORK CENTER FIELD.
009100*
009200*        5.  A DIFFERENT FORMS FILE IS MAINTAINED FOR AKRON AND THE
009300*            PLANTS.  THE AKRON VERSION HAS A "WORK CENTER" FIELD.
009400*            THE PLANT VERSION HAS THIS FIELD, BUT IT IS DISPLAY
009500*            ONLY, NO ENHANCEMENTS (INVISIBLE).  (THUS THE SCREEN
009600*            BUFFER IS THE SAME IN THE PROGRAM).  THE AKRON VERSION
009700*            HAS A 1 BYTE "CHARGE TYPE FIELD".  THE PLANTS VERSION
009800*            HAS A 2 BYTE EXTENSION TO THE CHARGE DEPT.  SO ON
009900*            THE AKRON FORM FILE, THE SECOND HALF THE THIS EXTENSION
010000*            FIELD WAS CHANGED TO  DISPLAY ONLY, NO ENHANCEMENTS.
010100*            (ONCE AGAIN, SO THAT THE SCREEN BUFFER DOES NOT NEED
010200*            TO BE DIFFERENT FOR THE TWO VERSIONS).
010300*             CIH.
010400*
010500*    ON OCT 27, 1984, CHANGED THIS SUBPROGRAM TO BE CALLED
010600*    BY THE NEW MAIN PROGRAM "TRMCORR". THIS PROGRAM WILL BE
010700*    DOING SPECIAL ISSUES AND RETURNS (SINGLE ITEM ONLY),
010800*    DESIGNATED "BANBURY EXPLOSION CORRECTIONS".  THESE
010900*    TRANSACTIONS ARE IDENTICAL TO NORMAL ISSUES AND RETURNS,
011000*    EXCEPT THAT THE WORKORDER FIELD IS USED TO HOLD THE
011100*    PRODUCTION DATE OF THE BANBURY EXPLOSION BEING
011200*    CORRECTED.  FOR EXAMPLE, ON JANUARY 1, THE USER MAY BE
011300*    DOING CORRECTIONS TO BANBURY PRODUCTION DONE ON
011400*    DECEMBER 31.  THE REASON THE PRODUCTION DATE MUST BE
011500*    ENTERED IS BECAUSE THE PLANTS WANT USAGE TO BE UPDATED
011600*    BY THE ACTUAL PRODUCTION DATE, AND THEY WANT THE MONTH
011700*    END PROCESSING TO BE CUT OFF BY PRODUCTION DATE ALSO.
011800*    IN THIS WAY, ANY USAGE FIGURES FOR ANY MONTH ON THE HP
011900*    SHOULD MATCH THE USAGE AS REPORTED BY THE PLANT'S
012000*    ACCOUNTING PROGRAMS.  ALSO, FOR MONTH END PROCESSING,
012100*    BANBURY EXPLOSION CORRECTIONS WILL BE HELD BACK OR LET
012200*    THRU BASED ON ACTUAL PRODUCTION DATE.  CIH.
012300*
012400*    ON JANUARY 9, 1984, ADDED A FIELD TO SHOW THE AVAILABLE
012500*    ONHAND QUANTITY TO THE ISSUE SINGLE/RETURN SINGLE SCREEN.
012600*    CIH.
012700*
012800*    ON JANUARY 23, 1985, CHANGED THE "K-TERMINAL" PARAMETER
012900*    (THE TERMINAL NUMBER OBTAINED FROM "TSPLPRT", WHICH IS PASSED
013000*    BACK AND FORTH TO "TIRMAIN") FROM 9(2) TO 9(4).  CIH.
013100*
013200*    ON MARCH 23, 1985, CHANGED THE PROGRAM TO BE FLEXIBLE FOR
013300*    EUROPEAN DATE FORMATS BY CALLING THE SUBPROGRAM "TDATECHK"
013400*    TO HANDLE ALL DATE WORK.  THE DATE WILL APPEAR IN EUROPEAN
013500*    FORMAT ON THE PRINTOUT IF AT A EUROPEAN PLANT (AS DETERMINED
013600*    BY THE SUBPROGRAM BY CHECKING FOR THE EXISTENCE OF THE
013700*    FILE "DDATECOD/DONTPURG.PUB").  FOR THE BANBURY CORRECTION
013800*    MODE, THE PRODUCTION DATE WILL BE EDITED BY THE SUBPROGRAM
013900*    ALSO, ALLOWING EUROPEAN PLANTS TO ENTER THE DATE AS
014000*    DAY, MONTH, YEAR, AND AMERICAN PLANTS TO ENTER THE DATE AS
014100*    MONTH, DAY, YEAR.  CIH.
014200*
014300*   10/08/85  ADDED CALLS TO FINDJCW, NLAPPEND, CATOPEN, AND
014400*             CATCLOSE IN ORDER TO ACCOMODATE THE NATIVE
014500*             LANGUAGE SUPPORT FACILITY.  ADDED LINKAGES AND
014600*             ALSO MADE THE CHANGE TO THE FORMFILE NAMES.
014700*   10/08/85  CHANGED ALL REFERENCES OF TSCRPRNT TO TSCRPRT2,
014800*             TDATECHK TO TDATECK2.
014900*             THIS WAS TO INCORPORATE THE NATIVE LANGUAGE
015000*             SUPPORT VERSIONS OF THESE SUBROUTINES.
015100*                                            -TW COTTON.
015200*
015300*   06/17/86  TOOK OUT CALL TO "TBLDSDTA", WHICH GOT DESCRIPTION
015400*             AS WELL AS SET UP BIN DISPLAY, AND REPLACED WITH CALL
015500*             TO "CDESC" TO GET THE NEW DESCRIPTION INFO IN THE
015600*             "DMANPART" DATASET.  CIH.
015700*
015800*
015900*      DATE 6/19/86                 A.M. KRAUSS
016000*         1. HARD-CODED ESCAPE SEQUENCES REMOVED FROM
016100*            PROGRAM.  THEY ARE NOW TO BE EXTERNALLY
016200*            SUPPLIED.
016300*         2. THE MAIN PROGRAM IN A JOB STREAM WILL
016400*            COPY ESC-NAM2 THAT CONTAINS THE HP
016500*            ESCAPE SEQUENCES.  IT WILL ALSO CALL
016600*            TESCSEQ THAT CONTAINS THE NON-HP ESCAPE
016700*            SEQUENCES, IF ANY ARE USED.  THE NON-HP
016800*            SEQUENCES WILL OVERRIDE THE HP SEQUENCES.
016900*         3. THE ACTUAL PRINTING PROGRAM WILL GET THE
017000*            APPROPRIATE SEQUENCES PASSED DOWN TO IT
017100*            THRU THE INTERMEDIATE SUBROUTINES THAT
017200*            COPY ESC-NAME.
017300*C
017300*C  08-25-92   BK DISMUKES  REQUEST# 6252
017300*C     1. ADDED LOGIC TO PASS STR-RESTRICTED-FLG TO TIREDIT.
017300*C
017300*C  10-23-92   BK DISMUKES  REQUEST# 6015
017300*C     1. ADDED LOGIC TO DISPLAY ONHAND FOR EACH STOREROOM
017300*C        LOCATION
      *C
      *C   04NOV1994    WILL MCINTYRE   REQUEST 94-027
      *C     ADDED CODE TO PASS NEW PARMS TO TQTYEDIT, TO CHECK FOR LIMITS
      *C     ON STOREROOM RETURNS.
      *C
      *C   AUGUST 1996  JEFF BUNGO
      *C     EXPAND DATE FIELDS FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C     INCLUDE CENTURY ON ACTIVITY AND ISSUE DATES.
017300*C
      *C   MAY 2, 1997  JEFF BUNGO
      *C     WRITE TC333/433 FOR EACH OWNER OF A BIN THAT AN
      *C     ISSUE IS MADE FROM.  DISPLAY OWNER OF BINS ON
      *C     THE WITHDRAWL SCREEN.  EDITS TO FORCE ISSUE FROM
      *C     GOODYEAR BINS FIRST MADE IN TQTYEDIT.
      *C
      *C   JULY 22, 1997 JEFF BUNGO
      *C     IF DISPLAYING A QUANTITY ERROR REPLACE ZERO QUANTITIES
      *C     WITH SPACES.  THIS IS TO AVOID ERRORS IN DATA
      *C     ENTRY WHERE THE ZEROS ARE NOT FIELD EXITED.
017300*C
      *C   OCTOBER 1995  JIM COFFMAN
      *C     CHANGED ISSPARTS PARAMETERS TO BE INCLUDED IN A COPYLIB
      *C     MEMBER. THIS WAS NECESSARY TO ALLOW THE AREA TO BE
      *C     EXPANDABLE TO CONTAIN THE LINK TO A WORK ORDER LOGIC
      *C     REQUEST NOW AVAILABLE IN AN E1 REQUISITION CREATE.
      *C
      *C   SEPT 22, 1998  CA YODER
      *C     ADDED CALL TO MCXSNDMSG TO SEND A MESSAGE TO USERS
      *C     SPECIFIED IN MCFPCSUSER FILE WHEN A PARTICULAR CODE
      *C     IS WITHDRAWN FROM THE STOREROOM.
      *C
017400 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
